# =====================================================================
# FORGE-AI :: Trivy misconfiguration suppressions
# =====================================================================
# Every entry here is a deliberate exception with a reason. Nothing is
# suppressed to make a check go green.
#
# Passed explicitly to the scan via the `trivyignores` input in
# .github/workflows/security.yml rather than relying on Trivy finding
# this file on its own.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# DS-0002  "Image user should not be 'root'"
#
#   Triggered by compose/samba/Dockerfile, which has no USER because
#   smbd must be root to bind port 445 and to switch to the guest
#   account. This is the one container in the stack that runs as root,
#   it is documented in docs/SECURITY.md, and the share it serves is
#   read-only, anonymous and carries no secret -- the per-host answer
#   file travels through wimboot, never through SMB.
#
#   Suppressing this by id is global rather than path-scoped, and that
#   is acceptable here because the Dockerfile text is NOT the control.
#   The control is the "Confirm the image does not run as root" step in
#   the containers job: it inspects the BUILT image and fails for
#   state-service and webhook, allowing only samba by name. That check
#   is strictly stronger than this rule -- it would catch a root user
#   arriving from a base image, which reading the Dockerfile cannot.
#
#   Both spellings are listed because Trivy reports this rule as
#   `DS-0002` in its own output and as `AVD-DS-0002` in SARIF, and the
#   project documentation is not reachable from this environment to
#   settle which form the ignore file matches. An id that matches
#   nothing is a no-op, so listing both is safe; the next run's
#   "Name the configuration findings" step reports whether it took.
DS-0002
AVD-DS-0002
